it's an image at odds with the country's  healthy environmentally friendly  reputation but for years switzerland's  been a haven for tobacco firms with some  of the most lax laws in europe  sunday's referendums changed things with  voters defying the government and  approving a ban on tobacco advertising  and newspapers the internet anywhere  young people can see them  it's laughable that for two years now a  health policy to fight covert 19 has  been in place and now we really have the  opportunity to introduce a new health  policy yet the swiss government has  advised people to vote no for me it's  obvious that we have to vote yes to the  ban those backing the ban say the  government's opposition is down to the  presence of the world's major tobacco  companies several have their  headquarters here and the industry  generates more than six billion dollars  a year for the swiss economy but the old  economic arguments no longer hold sway  there are nine thousand smoking related  deaths a year in the country  the impact on its health system is now  at the forefront of people's minds  i voted in favor of banning tobacco  advertising on minors i think the only  argument of the opponents was the  collapse of the swiss economy i don't  see how it is linked maybe i didn't  understand well but it seems more  important to me to protect children from  tobacco  the tobacco firms have lobbied hard to  avoid the ban with opponents claiming  cake and even sausages could face  similar restrictions but the campaign  failed to convince most people swiss  voters showing politicians and big  business that it's time to get tougher  on tobacco  neve barker al jazeera
 

